# Analyst Notes

Successful authentication events form the foundation of identity monitoring within a SOC. While Event ID 4624 is generated frequently during normal operations, correlating successful logons with privilege assignments, PowerShell execution, scheduled tasks, service creation, or unusual authentication patterns significantly improves detection fidelity.

This detection serves as a baseline for identifying suspicious authentication behavior and supports investigations involving account compromise, insider threats, and lateral movement.
